Hello,<div><br></div><div>I wanted to propose an idea for a function to start with a clean workspace.  </div><div><br></div><div>This is something that I like to do when I&#39;m testing scripts / package development to make sure that I have not inadvertently attached a library and unintentionally created a dependency.</div><div><br></div><div>I do something like this at the start of my scripts</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">source(&#39;<span style="font-size:13px">DetachNonStandardPackages.R&#39;)  ## actually I do </span><span style="font-size:13px">library(&#39;my_private_library&#39;)</span></font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">DetachNonStandardPackages()<br></font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">rm(list=ls())</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace"><br></font></div><div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">library(&#39;package1&#39;)</font></div></div><div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">library(&#39;package2&#39;)</font></div></div><div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">library(&#39;package3&#39;)</font></div></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">## etc...</font></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s what the function looks like:</div><div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">DetachNonStandardPackages = function(</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">    standard_packages = c(&#39;rstudio&#39;, &#39;stats&#39;, &#39;graphics&#39;, &#39;grDevices&#39;, &#39;utils&#39;, </font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">                          &#39;datasets&#39;, &#39;methods&#39;, &#39;base&#39;),</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">    special_packages = NULL</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">    ){</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">    </font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">    ## Some packages, like DTW can only be loaded once per R session, </font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">    ## don&#39;t detach those</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">    #special_packages = c(&#39;dtw&#39;, &#39;proxy&#39;)</font></div><div><span style="white-space:pre"><font face="courier new, monospace">	</font></span></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">    attached_packages = .packages()</font></div><div><span style="white-space:pre"><font face="courier new, monospace">	</font></span></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace"><span style="white-space:pre">	</span>cat(&#39;
Detaching non-standard libraries:
&#39;)</font></div><div><span style="white-space:pre"><font face="courier new, monospace">	</font></span></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace"><span style="white-space:pre">	</span>for(pkg in attached_packages){</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace"><span style="white-space:pre">		</span>if(! (pkg %in% standard_packages || pkg %in% special_packages) ){</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace"><span style="white-space:pre">			</span>cat(&#39;Detaching:&#39;, pkg, &#39;
&#39;)</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace"><span style="white-space:pre">			</span>detach(paste(&#39;package:&#39;, pkg, sep=&#39;&#39;), character.only=TRUE)</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace"><span style="white-space:pre">		</span>}</font></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace"><span style="white-space:pre">	</span>}</font></div><div><span style="white-space:pre"><font face="courier new, monospace">	</font></span></div><div><font face="courier new, monospace">}</font></div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>
